WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.688
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:15.042
Unit seven: Fashion Trends. Today you will talk about fashion using the present passive.

4
00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:18.076
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.905
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.519
Trend.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:28.410
Trend means a new style that many people follow.

8
00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:31.237
Wide trousers are a big trend this year.

9
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.340
Your turn. Say: Trend.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.015
Trend.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.623
Vintage.

12
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:43.499
Vintage means old but high quality and stylish.

13
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.688
I bought a vintage jacket.

14
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.820
Your turn. Say: Vintage.

15
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.586
Vintage.

16
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.734
Statement piece.

17
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.050
Statement piece means one bold item that people notice.

18
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.812
Her red bag is a statement piece.

19
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:05.475
Your turn. Say: Statement piece.

20
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:09.752
Statement piece.

21
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:11.495
Designer.

22
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:15.005
Designer means a person who creates clothes.

23
00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:17.697
She wants to be a fashion designer.

24
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:20.936
Your turn. Say: Designer.

25
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.813
Designer.

26
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:26.783
Influencer.

27
00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:31.281
Influencer means a person online who affects what people buy.

28
00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:34.266
That influencer has a million followers.

29
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.421
Your turn. Say: Influencer.

30
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.523
Influencer.

31
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:43.714
Sustainable fashion.

32
00:01:44.717 --> 00:01:48.400
Sustainable fashion means clothes made in ways that protect the planet.

33
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:51.401
Sustainable fashion uses less water.

34
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:55.226
Your turn. Say: Sustainable fashion.

35
00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.613
Sustainable fashion.

36
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.351
Thrift.

37
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.895
Thrift means to buy used clothes cheaply.

38
00:02:05.483 --> 00:02:07.657
I love to thrift at the Russian Market.

39
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.531
Your turn. Say: Thrift.

40
00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.310
Thrift.

41
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:15.981
Runway.

42
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:20.225
Runway means the stage where models show new clothes.

43
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:22.619
The models walked down the runway.

44
00:02:23.217 --> 00:02:25.753
Your turn. Say: Runway.

45
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.543
Runway.

46
00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.168
Seasonal.

47
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:34.392
Seasonal means for one time of the year.

48
00:02:34.983 --> 00:02:36.890
These are seasonal colours for summer.

49
00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:39.938
Your turn. Say: Seasonal.

50
00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.766
Seasonal.

51
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:45.460
Iconic.

52
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.587
Iconic means very famous and easy to recognise.

53
00:02:50.183 --> 00:02:52.520
The krama is an iconic Khmer scarf.

54
00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:55.653
Your turn. Say: Iconic.

55
00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.431
Iconic.

56
00:03:00.183 --> 00:03:01.324
Minimalist.

57
00:03:02.317 --> 00:03:05.744
Minimalist means simple, with very few details.

58
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.371
I like a minimalist style: white and black.

59
00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:12.473
Your turn. Say: Minimalist.

60
00:03:15.333 --> 00:03:16.462
Minimalist.

61
00:03:17.217 --> 00:03:17.962
Bold.

62
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:21.611
Bold means bright and strong, easy to notice.

63
00:03:22.217 --> 00:03:23.798
He wears bold colours.

64
00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:27.198
Your turn. Say: Bold.

65
00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:30.825
Bold.

66
00:03:31.633 --> 00:03:35.005
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.302
Visal, what fashion trends do you follow?

68
00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:43.462
I like vintage clothes. They are worn again by many teenagers.

69
00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.702
Where do you buy them?

70
00:03:46.817 --> 00:03:51.895
I thrift at local markets. Second-hand clothes are sold very cheaply there.

71
00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:54.797
That's sustainable fashion!

72
00:03:55.883 --> 00:04:00.161
Exactly. It is being promoted by my favorite influencer.

73
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.079
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:03.917 --> 00:04:06.485
Grammar focus: Present passive.

75
00:04:06.785 --> 00:04:08.018
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:08.717 --> 00:04:10.554
Vintage clothes are worn again.

77
00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.844
Sustainable fashion is being promoted.

78
00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.156
These shirts are made by local designers.

79
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.400
Use the passive when the action is more important than who does it.

80
00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:25.464
Be careful! Don't say: Vintage clothes are wear again.

81
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.294
Say: Vintage clothes are worn again.

82
00:04:30.594 --> 00:04:34.160
The passive needs the past participle: wear, wore, worn.

83
00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:37.747
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:38.533 --> 00:04:40.057
Thrift Is the New Trend.

85
00:04:40.357 --> 00:04:44.121
Vintage and sustainable fashion are becoming popular trends.

86
00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.876
Many clothes are made cheaply and thrown away quickly.

87
00:04:48.867 --> 00:04:51.934
Now, thrift shopping is being promoted by influencers.

88
00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:57.220
My favorite influencer prefers thrift shops to designer runway pieces.

89
00:04:58.233 --> 00:05:02.532
Her minimalist style and one bold statement piece are copied by many teenagers.

90
00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:07.681
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:10.586
Vintage clothes blank worn again.

92
00:05:10.886 --> 00:05:13.994
A, are. B, is. C, be.

93
00:05:17.533 --> 00:05:19.626
The answer is A: are.

94
00:05:20.783 --> 00:05:23.294
To buy used clothes cheaply is to blank.

95
00:05:23.594 --> 00:05:26.957
A, thrift. B, design. C, trend.

96
00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.233
The answer is A: thrift.

97
00:05:33.383 --> 00:05:36.138
Simple, with very few details, is blank.

98
00:05:36.438 --> 00:05:40.045
A, minimalist. B, bold. C, iconic.

99
00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.646
The answer is A: minimalist.

100
00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:50.078
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:53.357
What fashion trend do you follow or avoid?

102
00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.674
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:03.974 --> 00:06:12.352
I follow the vintage trend. Old shirts are sold cheaply at the market, and they are good for the planet. I avoid fast fashion.

104
00:06:12.652 --> 00:06:14.327
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:15.217 --> 00:06:19.332
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present passive.

106
00:06:19.632 --> 00:06:24.920
Today's value is sustainable living. Buy less, reuse more, and protect our planet.

107
00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.663
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

108
00:06:27.963 --> 00:06:31.057
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

